    "text": "# Engineering Handbook: Incident Response for AquaCore Control Systems (ACCS)\n\n**Document ID:** ACCS-IR-2024-01\n**Version:** 3.2\n**Classification:** Internal Engineering / Critical Infrastructure\n**Applicability:** All AquaCore Control Service (ACS) engineers, operators, and incident commanders.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Introduction and Scope\n\n### 1.1 Purpose\nThis handbook defines the standardized procedures for detecting, analyzing, mitigating, and recovering from incidents affecting the AquaCore Control Service (ACCS). ACCS is the central SCADA (Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition) and IoT management layer for municipal water treatment plants, distribution pumps, and reservoir monitoring systems.\n\n### 1.2 Criticality\nWater treatment is a **Life-Safety Critical** system. Incidents are not merely IT outages; they are potential public health hazards.\n*   **P1 (Critical):** Loss of visibility/control over chlorine dosing, pH balancing, or raw water intake. Immediate risk of contamination or system failure.\n*   **P2 (High):** Loss of secondary monitoring, telemetry gaps >15 minutes, or non-critical pump control failure.\n*   **P",
